<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George IV of Georgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1191">1191</a>–<a href="/years/1223">1223</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Lasha Giorgi, George IV Lasha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George IV, known as Lasha Giorgi, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1213 to 1223, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>. He continued his mother's wars against neighbouring Muslim rulers and planned to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a>, but in 1221 a Mongol force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> defeated him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-khunan">Khunan</a>. He died in 1223, reportedly of wounds received in the fighting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-iv-of-georgia.jpg" alt="George IV of Georgia" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This work is in the public domain in its country of origin and other countries a... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giorgi_IV_Lasha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
